    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI am not able to use `gcc` to comment out a line or a block of text anymore.\r\n\r\nWhenever I try, this I will get the following error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:160: nvim_exec(): Vim(lua):E5108: Error executing lua ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:392: attempt to call field 'get_filetypes' (a nil value) stack traceback: ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:392: in function 'traverse' ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:403: in function 'get_commentstring' ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:345: in function 'make_comment_parts' ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:215: in function 'toggle_lines' [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk [C]: in function 'cmd' ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:160: in function 'operator' [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk stack traceback: [C]: in function 'cmd' ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:160: in function 'operator' [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-1184+g0ecb4d725\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUsing `lazyvim`:\r\n\r\n`nvim <file>`\r\n\r\n`gcc` a line, or `gc` a visual selection.\r\n\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe line/selection should get commented.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNothing happens except the error described above.",
