            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nIs there a reason you still use development version of Neovim 0.9 even though there was already an official release? The error is there because 'mini.comment' uses some functionality from Neovim 0.9 **if** it can detect that version. In your case it detects it, but due to not being the released one it doesn't have a necessary functionality.\r\n\r\nI recommend either updating Neovim to current stable release 0.9 or downgrading to 0.8. Development versions of previous release are not supported.",
